ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "column screw pockets leave wood over them", 4, "mm of wood between a pocket's floor (2 deep: the head and hardware.col_pocket_clear) and the playing face, against hardware.col_pocket_skin"
ECHO: "DRC", "INFO", "key-board tail margin, least", 10.275, "mm past the last switch cutout that keeps the tail corners' pockets, heads and spacers clear of the last keys; boards.kb_tail_margin is 10.3"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "column standoffs clear of the chain headers", 29.7532, "mm from a standoff's hex, off its axis, to the nearest chain header and its plug, worst case - both boards' headers stand in the gap the standoffs span"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "key plate beyond the last key cutout", 20.14, "mm of aluminium; the plate stops short of the Matrix"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "oak lip under the frosted window", 2.4, "mm thick, 2 mm wide; the acrylic sits flush on it"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "rounded inside corners clear the caps and the LED array", [0.397918, 0.185786], "mm: a cap's corner, drawn square, to its slot's or recess's corner rounded to fabrication.corner_r_inner (stack.cap_clear a side; an MT165's own corner is rounded, so more); the LED array's corner to the window opening's"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "oak between the last cap slot and the window rebate", 28.4, "mm on the top face"
ECHO: "DRC", "NOTE", "LED tops to the frosted window's top face", 5.01, "mm - frosted acrylic this far above the LEDs softens the pixels; the owner chose it (2026-09-26)"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "etherCON body inside the cavity height", [6.55, 31.55, 6, 33], "body Z range vs cavity Z range at the tail, where the key plate has ended"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "key plate reaches past the column screws", 11.19, "mm of plate beyond the last column screw's head; the plate stops short of the Matrix"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "LED tops under the frosted window", 2.01, "mm, LED tops to the acrylic's underside - the Matrix on HDR-MATRIX's plastic on its carrier, hung from the oak (drc.echo 'Matrix carrier hangs from the oak')"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "LED array fits the window opening it stands in", 1.2, "mm across, opening less the array"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "etherCON flange fits behind the tail cap", 6.55, "mm, the smaller of above and below the flange, inside the cap's height"
ECHO: "DRC", "NOTE", "tail cap material below and above the etherCON bore", [8.05, 8.95], "mm - the connector stands on the floor, so it is not centred"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "MIDI jack in the oak bottom", [2.5, 12, 3.5, 2, [2.5, 2.3, 3.15, 3.15, 11.4], 14.8], "mm: the oak the nut clamps (at most the thread past the collar less the nut, 2.5 [ds SAMESKY-SJ5-43502PM.pdf p.2]; at least 2); the counterbore from inside, across and deep; the thread and nut standing proud of the bottom face; the counterbore's oak to the etherCON's footprint, to the side's groove, to the adapter's front face and to the tail cap (against 1), and its edge past the bottom plate's end (against 0); the tabs' top under the oak top's underside (against 2)"
ECHO: "DRC", "NOTE", "MIDI jack lead to J-MIDI", 40.15, "mm of CBL-MIDI from the jack's tabs to J-MIDI: the run through its bends, 25.15, plus midi.lead_slack"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "tail cap recess for the etherCON inside the tail face", 2, "mm of oak round the 3 mm recess that leaves the NE8FAV its 3 mm panel (ethercon.panel_max 3)"
ECHO: "DRC", "NOTE", "etherCON PUSH tab against the tail face", 0.8, "mm the tab stands proud of the tail face (negative = inside the recess)"
ECHO: "DRC", "NOTE", "etherCON locating pegs, cut off flush", 0.95, "mm the two pegs under the flange would reach into the oak bottom if left on (ethercon.peg_below; ADR 0021)"
ECHO: "DRC", "INFO", "logo: the band it sits in and its size", [[6, 41], 35, [20.1564, 27.486], [23.5, 28.5]], "mm: the band along the body (the mouth cap's inside face to the first cap slot) and its length; the mark's extent along x across at scale 0.509 turned 90 deg (its top to the mouth); its centre"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "logo fits its band (seam, cap slot, edge roundovers)", [7.4218, 7.4218, 13.257, 13.257], "mm of plain oak from the mark's extent to the mouth cap's seam, to the first cap slot, and to each long edge's roundover flat, against logo.margin_min; the largest scale that keeps it is 0.732323"
ECHO: "DRC", "PASS", "logo etch leaves wood over the column screw pockets", [3, 2.41045, 9.26901], "mm: the oak between the etch's floor (1 deep) and a pocket's (2 up from below), against hardware.col_pocket_skin - so it holds wherever they meet in plan; then the nearest pocket's clearance in plan to the mark's extent (negative = under its bounding box) and to the ring's outside edge"
ECHO: "DRC", "NOTE", "logo: smallest gap in the etch", 1.018, "mm of oak between two etched parts at scale 0.509, against logo.laser_min_gap 1; under the mark's own 2 at 100 % (branding/README.md, the laser guideline), so the etch test on an offcut (ROADMAP) confirms it holds and the two pours stay apart"
ECHO: "DRC", "NOTE", "logo etch depth and fill", [1, "epoxy"], "mm, and what fills it (branding/README.md 'Colour fill': deeper than a plain burn, so the epoxy keys in)"
